  "headline": "157 of 157 books with a local body under 2 KB have an upstream source that is equally short. Zero are our defect. In EVERY record local == upstream exactly, byte for byte.",
  "what_this_settles": "The rate question raised by two anecdotes. gid 4715 (4 bytes upstream) and gid 9320 (66 bytes) were real but not evidence of a systemic extraction failure \u2014 they are the low end of a population of genuinely short or textless Gutenberg records: symphony scores, MIDI files, photo collections, software manuals, single carols.",
  "extractor_verdict": "Faithful. Not one book in the suspect set lost text that upstream had.",
